+    a coin's name (here: an instruction) is in no line the node says in its own voice; a node that follows no coin is offered what it was offered before
+10 a line to a launch's node through the pages (/fun/p2p/TICKER)
+    3,000,000 random bytes to a node that says them back, through a follower's port, the pages' WebSocket and on to the node: the same bytes came back
+    a node sending 48 MB to a follower that reads nothing: after 4 s it had been let send 15.0 MB, after 7 s 15.0 MB (what the sockets in between hold); once the follower read, all 48 MB arrived, whole
+    a node that says 200,000 bytes and ends its sending: the follower read exactly those, then the end; a follower that sends 500,000 bytes and ends its sending: the node read exactly those, then the end, and the 70,000 bytes it answered with arrived
+    a ticker the site does not serve, one whose port is not a node's (22): 404; not a WebSocket: 426; a request that names a host and a port beside the ticker still reaches the site's own node of that launch and nothing else
